sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Student / Administrator
    participant Client as React 18 SPA Client
    participant Router as Express Auth Router
    participant Ctrl as Auth Controller
    participant Security as Bcrypt & JWT Service
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas (users)
    participant Blacklist as TokenBlacklist (TTL Index)

    Note over User,Blacklist: PHASE 1: DUAL-CHANNEL AUTHENTICATION & SESSION INITIATION
    User->>Client: Enters email & password, clicks "Login"
    Client->>Router: POST /api/auth/login {email, password}
    Router->>Ctrl: execute login(req, res)
    Ctrl->>DB: findOne({ email: normalizedEmail })
    DB-->>Ctrl: Returns User Document (with passwordHash)
    Ctrl->>Security: bcrypt.compare(password, passwordHash)
    Security-->>Ctrl: Password verification successful (true)
    Ctrl->>Security: signJWT({ id, role, jti: uuid() }, secret, 7d)
    Security-->>Ctrl: Generates Signed Cryptographic JWT
    Ctrl-->>Router: Set-Cookie: token (HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure)
    Router-->>Client: 200 OK { success: true, token, user: profileData }
    Client-->>User: Navigate to /dashboard (Session Established)

    Note over User,Blacklist: PHASE 2: SUBSEQUENT PROTECTED REQUEST VERIFICATION
    User->>Client: Accesses protected view (/arena or /profile)
    Client->>Router: GET /api/user/profile (Cookie + Authorization Bearer)
    Router->>Blacklist: findOne({ token: hashedToken })
    Blacklist-->>Router: null (Token is not revoked)
    Router->>Security: jwt.verify(token, secret)
    Security-->>Router: Valid Decoded Claims { id, role }
    Router-->>Client: 200 OK { profileData }

    Note over User,Blacklist: PHASE 3: SECURE LOGOUT & SERVER-SIDE TOKEN REVOCATION
    User->>Client: Clicks "Sign Out" button
    Client->>Router: POST /api/auth/logout (Bearer Token + Cookie)
    Router->>Ctrl: execute logout(req, res)
    Ctrl->>Blacklist: create({ token: hashedToken, userId, expiresAt })
    Blacklist-->>Ctrl: Revocation recorded (TTL auto-cleanup active)
    Ctrl-->>Router: Clear-Cookie: token (maxAge: 0, path: '/')
    Router-->>Client: 200 OK { message: "Session successfully invalidated" }
    Client->>Client: Flush AuthContext & purge scoped drafts
    Client-->>User: Redirect to /login (Session terminated)